{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af164e1","nodeId":"woemCQmWTR-hIoWAci3d5","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# Volume Mounts\n\nVolume mounts are a way to map a folder or file on the host system to a folder or file inside a container. This allows the data to persist outside the container even when the container is removed. Additionally, multiple containers can share the same volume, making data sharing between containers easy.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Docker Volumes","url":"https://docs.docker.com/storage/volumes/","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba72"},{"type":"official","title":"Docker Volume Flags","url":"https://docs.docker.com/storage/bind-mounts/#choose-the--v-or---mount-flag","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba73"},{"type":"video","title":"Docker Volumes explained in 6 minutes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p2PH_YPCsis","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba74"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/woemCQmWTR-hIoWAci3d5.md"}